  {
    "sha": "e58bcfc7b474f606f73c735a880df3a951951a93",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGU1OGJjZmM3YjQ3NGY2MDZmNzNjNzM1YTg4MGRmM2E5NTE5NTFhOTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-14T00:35:26Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-14T00:35:26Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): open the browser file chooser inside the user's click (Safari)\n\nSafari opens a file chooser only while the user's click is being\nhandled. eframe runs the frame that sees a mouse release inside its\npointerup handler, but the web shell drained the queued Open model /\nOpen project actions at the start of the NEXT frame, from\nrequestAnimationFrame, where Safari ignores input.click() without a\nword. The web shell now runs a queue holding a chooser action at the\nend of the clicked frame (State::run_click_actions), still inside\npointerup. The hidden input is attached to the page (display:none, the\nMDN pattern) and removed when replaced. A chooser asked for outside a\nclick (the Cmd/Ctrl+O shortcut) says on the status line what to do if\nthe browser refused it. The browser build no longer starts with \"no\ntheme folder found beside the exe\".\n\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
